<description>
Swap a connector segment with repeated marker sprites by connecting the marker anchors and stamping the sprite at the segment endpoints.

Input structure
The grid has one background color and exactly two foreground colors. One foreground color forms a single straight 8-connected segment. The other foreground color forms two or more identical centered sprites.

Rule
Build a background canvas of the same size. Draw straight connector-color segments between every pair of original sprite anchors. Then stamp the marker sprite, using its centered anchor, onto the two endpoints of the original connector segment.

Key insight
The original segment endpoints are the destinations for the repeated sprite, while the original sprite centers become the vertices of the new connector-color complete graph.
</description>
<annotation>
{
  "type": "move_along_path",
  "src": "single straight connector segment c and repeated centered marker sprites s",
  "path": "for every pair of s.center anchors, the row/column/45-degree segment between them",
  "trajectory": "paint each full path with c.color on a background canvas",
  "transform": "erase original foreground; stamp one copy of s centered on each endpoint of c"
}
</annotation>
<generation_spec>
```yaml
spec:
  grid: 11-16 rows x 11-16 cols (square)
  background: single color (always 7 in eval) [observed]
  foreground_colors: exactly 2 distinct non-bg colors
  connector:
    shape: single straight 8-connected segment (horizontal, vertical, or 45-degree diagonal)
    length: 6-10 cells
    color: one of the two fg colors; forms exactly 1 connected component
  sprites:
    count: 2-3 identical copies of a single shape
    placement_ratio: HIGH triangle case; about 3/4 of eval inputs have exactly 3 copies arranged as a non-collinear triangle, with 2-copy cases as the minority
    no_three_collinear: REQUIRED; when there are 3 copies, their anchors must not be collinear
    color: the other fg color; each copy is a separate 8-connected component
    bbox: odd height x odd width (1x1 to 5x3)
    center_anchor: bbox center cell must be part of the sprite
    symmetry: LR and UD [observed]
    anchor_alignment: every pair of sprite anchors must be connected by a valid straight 8-connected line (H/V/diagonal)
  constraints:
    no_overlap_input: connector cells and sprite cells do not overlap
    no_overlap_output: new connector lines (between anchors) and new sprites (at endpoints) do not overlap
    in_bounds_output: sprites stamped at connector endpoints must fit within grid
  transform:
    output: clear grid to bg; draw connector-color lines between all sprite anchor pairs; stamp sprite at each connector endpoint

generation_strategy:
  approach: output-first
  steps:
    1. Choose grid size (11-16, square), bg, two fg colors (connector_color, sprite_color).
    2. Design a centered sprite with odd bbox dims (1x1 to 5x5), LR+UD symmetric, center cell present. Compute radius = max offset from center.
    3. Place sprite anchors such that every pair is connected by a valid H/V/diagonal line. Prefer the dominant eval case: exactly 3 anchors forming a non-collinear triangle with axis-aligned/diagonal sides (~75% of samples). Generate 2-anchor cases as the minority. Do not generate 3-anchor collinear layouts.
    4. Choose a straight segment direction (H/V/diagonal) and length (6-10). Place the two endpoints so that stamping the sprite at each endpoint stays in bounds and does not overlap the connector lines drawn in step 3.
    5. Build the OUTPUT: draw connector-color lines between anchor pairs, stamp sprite at endpoints.
    6. Build the INPUT: stamp sprite copies at anchor positions, draw the connector segment between its endpoints. Verify no overlap between the two colors.
```
</generation_spec>
</reference_puzzle>

