<description>
Move the orange rectangle onto the maroon rectangle and mark gated corridor crossings in red.

Input structure
- The dominant background contains black obstacle segments.
- There is one solid orange rectangle and one solid maroon rectangle of the same size.
- The two rectangles share either their row span or their column span, so the move is straight and axis-aligned.

Rule
- Erase the original orange rectangle to the background.
- Replace the maroon rectangle with the orange rectangle.
- Between the two rectangles, paint red across the moving rectangle's width or height only at corridor cells flanked by black obstacle segments perpendicular to the movement.

Key insight
- The black segments define gates in the straight corridor; only those gated openings, not every swept background cell, become red.
</description>
<annotation>
{
  "type": "move_along_path",
  "src": "solid orange rectangle s",
  "path": "straight horizontal or vertical corridor from s to the aligned same-sized maroon rectangle d",
  "dst": "same-sized maroon rectangle d aligned with s on one axis",
  "trajectory": "paint red only at corridor openings flanked by black segments perpendicular to the path",
  "transform": "erase old s to background; replace d with orange; keep black segments and all other cells unchanged"
}
</annotation>
<generation_spec>
```yaml
spec:
  grid: 8-26 rows x 8-26 cols, always square [observed]
  background: magenta (6)
  colors: background + black (0) + orange (7) + maroon (9); output adds red (2)
  rectangles:
    count: 2 (one orange src, one maroon dst), same size
    shape: 1x1 to 4x4, always square [observed]
    alignment: share exactly one axis span (same rows XOR same cols), movement is axis-aligned
    corridor: straight bg-only gap between src and dst, length 5-7 cells
  gates:
    structure: pairs of black 1xN segments flanking the corridor perpendicularly, N=2 always [observed]
    symmetry: left/right (or top/bottom) walls always have gates at identical positions
    total: 2-8 gate pairs, some between rects (2-3), rest beyond as distractors (0-6)
    spacing: 2-4 cells between consecutive gate positions
    all black cells in the grid belong to gate pairs (no stray black)
  transform:
    - erase orange src to background
    - paint orange at maroon dst position
    - for each gate row/col strictly between the two rects, fill corridor cells red

generation_strategy:
  approach: output-first
  steps:
    1. Pick square grid size S in [8,26], square rect side R in [1,4], movement axis (H or V).
    2. Place the orange rect (output position = dst). Ensure room for corridor + src on the chosen axis.
    3. Place src position along the same axis, corridor length 5-7 cells away (same cross-axis span).
    4. Generate N_total gate positions (2-8) along the corridor axis, spaced 2-4 apart; at least 2 must fall strictly between src and dst (these become red). Others extend beyond as distractors.
    5. At each gate position, place a pair of 2-cell black segments flanking the corridor.
    6. Build output: orange at dst, red at gated corridor cells between src and dst, black segments unchanged.
    7. Build input: orange at src position, maroon at dst position, black segments unchanged, rest background.
