  17: def main(grid: np.ndarray) -> np.ndarray:
  18:     """
  19:     Recolor each 8-connected foreground object by whether its normalized shape is repeated or unique.
  20: 
  21:     Input structure
  22:     - The dominant background contains several same-color foreground objects.
  23:     - Objects are 8-connected; diagonal contact joins pixels into the same object.
  24:     - Up to translation within each bbox, exactly one object shape appears once
  25:       and exactly one other object shape appears multiple times.
  26: 
  27:     Rule
  28:     - Group foreground objects by their normalized bbox mask.
  29:     - Recolor the singleton-shape object red.
  30:     - Recolor every repeated-shape object blue.
  31:     - Keep the background unchanged.
  32: 
  33:     Key insight
  34:     - The recolor is determined by object-shape frequency, not by position or size alone.
  35:     """
